<%# Age result (spec issue #82, DESIGN.md §4 Hero-result + Stat grid): a surface card with
    a 5px coral left rule holding the calendar breakdown as the headline answer — the
    years / months / days the person has lived, each a big tabular-nums figure with its
    unit — and, beneath it, the same interval expressed four other ways (total months /
    weeks / days / hours) as a stat grid so one age reads every way at once. `calc:` is a
    valid Calculators::Age; result keys are years/months/days + the four totals (§4). %>
<% result = calc.result %>
<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
  <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
    <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Age</p>

      <%# The calendar breakdown — the headline. Three big figures (Y / M / D), each with
          its unit beneath, on the Affix/Grouped tiers so they read as one answer. The
          tabular-nums keeps the numerals aligned. %>
      <dl class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
        <% [ [ :years, "years" ], [ :months, "months" ], [ :days, "days" ] ].each do |key, unit| %>
          <div class="flex items-baseline gap-1.5">
            <dt class="sr-only"><%= unit %></dt>
            <dd class="text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= integer_display(result[key]) %></dd>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-label" aria-hidden="true"><%= unit %></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </dl>

      <%# A plain-language echo of the same breakdown (zero units dropped) so the answer
          reads as a sentence, not only as three figures. %>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted"><%= age_breakdown_phrase(result) %> old</p>

      <%# Total-unit conversions — the same interval four other ways, in the shared
          responsive stat grid (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid", issue #143): `.stat-grid` /
          `.stat-card` size each card to a min width and let the grid wrap/flow (≈4 across
          on a wide panel, collapsing to 2×2 when narrow). The card shell keeps even a large
          6+ digit Total hours (e.g. 306,792) in full; the value is whitespace-nowrap
          tabular-nums so it never wraps mid-number. %>
      <dl class="mt-6 stat-grid">
        <% age_total_units.each do |unit| %>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-faint">Total <%= unit[:label].downcase %></dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= integer_display(result[unit[:key]]) %></dd>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
